---
import Plate from '../../plate/Plate.astro';
import FilmControls from '../../plate/FilmControls.astro';
import FilmSubtitles from '../../plate/FilmSubtitles.astro';
import FilmTranscript from '../../plate/FilmTranscript.astro';
import '../../plate/film.css';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { STRONG_STILL, STRONG_STATS } from './data';
import { CUES, TIMELINE } from './story';
import './trapped-waves.css';

const formula = (tex: string) => renderFormula(tex, false);

const labels = [
  { id: 'spectrum', tex: String.raw`[-2d-h,\,2d+h]`, blue: false },
  { id: 'interval', tex: 'I_3', blue: true },
  { id: 'threshold', tex: String.raw`\lambda_3`, blue: true },
  { id: 'resolvent', tex: String.raw`(H-E-i\eta)^{-1}`, blue: true },
  { id: 'profile', tex: String.raw`u=\frac{\ln(r/r_0)}{\ln(R/r_0)}`, blue: false },
];

const peak = Math.max(...STRONG_STILL);

const strongEnd = STRONG_STATS.at(-1);

if (!strongEnd || peak <= 0) throw new Error('The no-JavaScript still needs the computed strong-disorder wave.');

const sites = STRONG_STILL.map((probability, index) => ({
  x: 32 + index % 31 * 7.8,
  y: 41 + Math.floor(index / 31) * 7.8,
  radius: Math.sqrt(probability / peak) * 3.5,
}));

const mapX = (energy: number) => 85 + energy / 14 * 65;

const mapY = (disorder: number) => 165 - disorder / 8 * 120;

const wedge = (dimension: number) => `M${mapX(-2 * dimension)} ${mapY(0)}L${mapX(-2 * dimension - 8)} ${mapY(8)}L${mapX(2 * dimension + 8)} ${mapY(8)}L${mapX(2 * dimension)} ${mapY(0)}Z`;
---

<Plate
  caption="An electron's wave on a grid, free without impurities and trapped by strong ones; the long-predicted map of trapped and spreading states; and the two claimed proofs: pure point spectrum in two dimensions, and a band of spreading states in three and up."
  leftOut="one dimension and diffusion; multiscale analysis, fractional moments and spectral averaging; the earlier partial results; the forms of the unknown disorder thresholds; Fourier and packing bounds; scattering-matrix clearing; resonant cells and the acceptance likelihood; the port hierarchy, screening and analytic test; other disorder laws and the Lean statement. The proof drawings are schematic."
>
  <uruk-trapped-waves class="film-host">
    <div class="twfilm">
      <div class="twfilm-stage" data-film-viewport>
        <canvas class="twfilm-canvas" data-film-canvas role="img" aria-label="A film of computed electron waves on a grid, comparing strong, medium and weak random disorder. A two-panel map distinguishes the claimed two-dimensional pure point result from the small absolutely continuous band in three dimensions. A complete text transcript follows."></canvas>
        <div class="twfilm-still" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="twfilm-still-grid">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 325" role="presentation">
              <text x="150" y="16" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="11">STRONG DISORDER · h = 8</text>
              {Array.from({ length: 31 }, (_, index) => (
                <>
                  <line x1={32 + index * 7.8} y1="41" x2={32 + index * 7.8} y2="275" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".35" stroke-opacity=".25" />
                  <line x1="32" y1={41 + index * 7.8} x2="266" y2={41 + index * 7.8} stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".35" stroke-opacity=".25" />
                </>
              ))}
              {sites.map((site) => <circle cx={site.x} cy={site.y} r={site.radius} fill="var(--ink)" />)}
              <circle cx="149" cy="158" r="23.4" fill="none" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width=".8" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
              <text x="150" y="296" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="12">WITHIN 3 SITES: {Math.round(strongEnd.within3 * 100)}%</text>
              <text x="150" y="317" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="13">Computed on 31 × 31 sites, at model time 40.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="twfilm-still-map">
            {[2, 3].map((dimension) => (
              <svg viewBox="0 0 170 220" role="presentation">
                <defs><pattern id={`twfilm-still-hatch-${dimension}`} width="6" height="6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M0 6L6 0" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".6" /></pattern></defs>
                <text x="85" y="14" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="13">{dimension === 2 ? '2D' : '3D AND UP'}</text>
                <text x="85" y="32" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="11">UNDER REVIEW</text>
                <path d={wedge(dimension)} fill={dimension === 2 ? `url(#twfilm-still-hatch-${dimension})` : 'none'} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width=".8" />
                {dimension === 3 && (
                  <>
                    <path d={`M${mapX(-14)} ${mapY(8)}L${mapX(-6)} ${mapY(0)}L${mapX(-4.6)} ${mapY(0)}L${mapX(-11)} ${mapY(8)}Z`} fill={`url(#twfilm-still-hatch-${dimension})`} />
                    <path d={`M${mapX(14)} ${mapY(8)}L${mapX(6)} ${mapY(0)}L${mapX(4.6)} ${mapY(0)}L${mapX(11)} ${mapY(8)}Z`} fill={`url(#twfilm-still-hatch-${dimension})`} />
                    <rect x={mapX(-6) + 1} y={mapY(1.1)} width="6" height={mapY(0) - mapY(1.1)} fill="var(--blue)" fill-opacity=".2" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
                  </>
                )}
                <line x1="17" y1="165" x2="155" y2="165" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".7" />
                <line x1="17" y1="165" x2="17" y2="43" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".7" />
                <text x="8" y="103" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">h</text>
                <text x="85" y="181" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">ENERGY</text>
                <text x="85" y="198" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="11">{dimension === 2 ? 'Claim: pure point for h > 0' : 'Claim: a small AC interval'}</text>
                <text x="85" y="214" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="10">{dimension === 2 ? 'No expert discussion found' : 'Interval widths schematic'}</text>
              </svg>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="twfilm-formulas" aria-hidden="true" data-bleed>
          {labels.map((label) => <span class:list={['twfilm-label', 'twfilm-label--small', { 'twfilm-label--blue': label.blue }]} data-label={label.id}><span set:html={formula(label.tex)} /></span>)}
          <span class="twfilm-label twfilm-status" data-label="status2d"><span>UNDER REVIEW</span></span>
          <span class="twfilm-label twfilm-status" data-label="status3d"><span>UNDER REVIEW</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <FilmSubtitles cues={CUES} />
    </div>
    <FilmControls id="twfilm-timeline" timeline={TIMELINE} />
    <FilmTranscript cues={CUES}>
      <p class="film-method">How the film is made. The free wave is computed from Bessel functions for the infinite square grid. The display is a crop, not a probability distribution renormalized to its window. At model time 7 the 31 × 31 crop contains about 97.69% of the probability. On phones, the 21 × 21 crop at time 4.5 contains about 98.11%. The rest lies outside the drawing. Within each frame, disc area is proportional to probability, with the largest disc setting the display scale. The pulled-back 201 × 201 map uses logarithmic ink shading so faint tails remain visible.</p>
      <p class="film-method">One uniform impurity sample on 201 × 201 sites, generated with NumPy's default random generator and seed 7, supplies every disorder strength. Strong disorder, h = 8, uses diagonalization of its central 31 × 31 box. Medium h = 5 and weak h = 2 use Chebyshev propagation on the larger box. The display interpolates computed probability snapshots. At h = 2 and time 400, the root-mean-square distance is about 43.36 sites and about 0.54% of the probability lies in the outer four rows and columns. This wave is still spreading. It is not shown as a numerical demonstration of weak-disorder trapping.</p>
      <p class="film-method">A finite box has discrete spectrum even without impurities. Its extended standing wave illustrates a spatial pattern; the absolutely continuous band belongs to the infinite-grid description. Multiplying an eigenstate by a global phase does not change its probability, so its discs remain still. The two-dimensional paper's pure point claim does not assert dynamical localization, exponential decay, a trap size, or one probability-one event for all disorder strengths simultaneously.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The spectrum outlines <span set:html={formula(String.raw`[-2d-h,\,2d+h]`)} /> are exact. The predicted regions, interval widths, mobility edge and resolvent curves are schematic. The trapped resolvent comparison tends to zero away from sharp eigenvalues, or at almost every energy; poles can occur at the eigenvalues. The binary digits are computed, while damping, failed trials and pending sites illustrate the proof's bookkeeping. Six digits illustrate refinement before the actual simulated values appear. The ports and probes are schematic. The logarithmic profile has continuum energy <span set:html={formula(String.raw`2\pi/\ln(R/r_0)`)} />, giving about 9.07, 4.53, 2.27 and 1.13 as the radius ratio is 2, 4, 16 and 256. Neither the finite simulations nor the drawings verify the infinite-volume proofs.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The family is under review because Jaksic and Last worked through a final step of the three-dimensional paper. That is not a verdict on its whole argument. The article's dated review found no named expert discussing the two-dimensional paper.</p>
    </FilmTranscript>
  </uruk-trapped-waves>
</Plate>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
